<body lang=3D"ZH-CN" link=3D"blue" vlink=3D"purple" style=3D"text-justify-t=
rim:punctuation">
<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-=
family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">Hi all,<o:p></o:p></span><=
/p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">This is the Fullpass Test Report for Yocto 1.2 M4 RC3 build. There are 6=
 new bugs found. The most critical one is for routerstationpro&nbsp;which
 blocked all cases on routerstationpro&nbsp;, reported as bug 2292; There a=
re 3 new minor bugs reported for build appliance, x32 and Hob, as bug 2324,=
 2300 and 2325; 2 bugs are new reported for ADT that libpseudo.so can=A1=AF=
t find GLIBC_2.14 and glxgears fail in qemux86/x86-64.<o:p></o:p></span></p=
>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">Except routerstationpro , all&nbsp;BSPs and QEMU targets work well witho=
ut major issue, there are 4 open bugs , they are: unable to set the
 static IP on all BSPs and qemu target, CPU utilization is high level after=
 standby on crownbay; I2C_transfer error on eMenlow and connman-property la=
unch with Glib-Gobject-warning on qemux86-64 image.
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">For Hob testing, it is based on master with commit 720fe9e371eef16da19df=
0885188aa0341ad2090, there is only minor issue found with it
 that =A1=B0View files=A1=B1 does not work on Ubuntu 11.04. All the other f=
unctions could work well.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">For ADT, except clutter, all features work well except the old bug
<span style=3D"color:black">32bit kernel generated oprofile data file can=
=A1=AFt be read by remote 64bit operation.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">For distribution testing, N&#43;1 testing is performed against CentOS/Ub=
untu/Opensuse/Fedora.<span style=3D"color:black"> The build issues
 on Fedora 17 Alpha and Opensuse 12.2 Milestone 2 still exist</span>.<o:p><=
/o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">For Core build feature, most functions could work, except for multilib. =
There are some new failures with multilib, which we do not submit
 bugs for them since developers already have fixing patches. Except for bui=
ld appliance, all the other components are based on RC3. Build appliance is=
 based on master with commit 720fe9e371eef16da19df0885188aa0341ad2090. Yoct=
o-bsp tool fails to create layer
 against json file since Tom=A1=AFs fixing patch is not in RC3 yet. <o:p></=
o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">For build performance, one qemux86 sato build on a Core i7 machine costs=
 110 minutes, which is almost the same as the result in 1.2
 M4 RC2 build(112 minutes)<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:21.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">Note: The test report is archived @
<a href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_1.2_Milestone_Test_Repo=
